response.body:
While optimizing timing constraints and attempting to specify realistic capacitive loads for the design's outputs, maliberty noted that the maximum capacitance is extremely low. For example, the maximum capacitance for the `sg13g2_IOPadOut4mA` cell is specified as follows:

```
 cell (sg13g2_IOPadOut4mA) {
    pin (pad) {
      direction : "output";
      max_capacitance : 1.1116;
```

From my understanding it should not be an exotic use-case to drive at least ~30pF of capacitive load from an output I/O cell, so I would expect the liberty to provide timing information and a maximum capacitance up to at least 50pF, maybe more.


Context/original discovery: https://github.com/The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD/discussions/8246#discussioncomment-14335759

